(3522315, 490359, 5822, '<td valign="top">Shutter speed appears to be critical for this photo as too fast would render the water not as attractive as the smooth flow of this photo and too slow would render the bird not as sharp as you''ve captured. My only gripe would be more light to have fallen on the bird''s body. Good job.</td>', 'Shutter speed appears to be critical for this photo as too fast would render the water not as attractive as the smooth flow of this photo and too slow would render the bird not as sharp as you''ve captured. My only gripe would be more light to have fallen on the bird''s body. Good job.', '2007-04-05 13:35:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(3522344, 490507, 5822, '<td valign="top">Great capture! Love it! The blown out highlights (was this intentional? my guess is not) and yellow toning really add to the dynamism and energy of this image, as does the flag and black sky. The speed limit sign adds a touch of irony in that it really refers to wind speed, and not to it''s usual designation. <br/> <br/>The person walking, however, appears too non-chalant for his surroundings and I think someone displaying a gesture of fighting the wind, bracing themselves or holding on to a hat would be more appropo and create greater impact. Finally, compositionally, I would prefer a less centered composition and think about about 1/2" could have been cropped off the left side. <br/> <br/>Was this photographed through car or house window? Even with the faults I''ve mentioned above, I''m giving this a 10 and adding it to my favorites. Thank you!</td>', 'Great capture! Love it! The blown out highlights (was this intentional? my guess is not) and yellow toning really add to the dynamism and energy of this image, as does the flag and black sky. The speed limit sign adds a touch of irony in that it really refers to wind speed, and not to it''s usual designation.  The person walking, however, appears too non-chalant for his surroundings and I think someone displaying a gesture of fighting the wind, bracing themselves or holding on to a hat would be more appropo and create greater impact. Finally, compositionally, I would prefer a less centered composition and think about about 1/2" could have been cropped off the left side.  Was this photographed through car or house window? Even with the faults I''ve mentioned above, I''m giving this a 10 and adding it to my favorites. Thank you!', '2007-04-05 13:52:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(3522394, 490130, 5822, '<td valign="top">Could be an interesting image as I like the vista/overlook, but it lacks contrast and sharpness, imo. Forground adds nothing to the picture, is ugly, especially the shrub, and takes away about 1/4 of the image real estate. Could you have moved forward to eliminate it? Deeper DOF would probably help sharpness. What aperture/f-stop did you use? Finally, it appears to need a color balance adjustment to reduce cyan. I hope you found my comments helpful and not hostile.</td>', 'Could be an interesting image as I like the vista/overlook, but it lacks contrast and sharpness, imo. Forground adds nothing to the picture, is ugly, especially the shrub, and takes away about 1/4 of the image real estate. Could you have moved forward to eliminate it? Deeper DOF would probably help sharpness. What aperture/f-stop did you use? Finally, it appears to need a color balance adjustment to reduce cyan. I hope you found my comments helpful and not hostile.', '2007-04-05 14:17:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(3522413, 490815, 13712, '<td valign="top">very nice...</td>', 'very nice...', '2007-04-05 14:24:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(3522448, 488982, 8139, '<td valign="top">nicely captured, good background colors</td>', 'nicely captured, good background colors', '2007-04-05 14:39:22.000000', NULL, 1),
