(3527740, 489740, 65886, '<td valign="top">excellent!!</td>', 'excellent!!', '2007-04-07 14:47:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(3527777, 486597, 50695, '<td valign="top">This is a great, great capture. It looks like a Picasso painting of a rodeo. Notice how the background is all texture. The horse looks like he''s praying. As he kneels into a prone position, the man is forced into a supine position, each being submissive in his own way. The fringe on the cowboy is excessive, but that becomes its own statement (perhaps on the feminine becoming masculine or the masculine becoming feminine or the sublime becoming ridiculous or the ridiculous becoming sublime... as we imagine the frilly cowboy when he is not in the middle of an intense act and mentally compare it to this one who is). I can imagine Picasso indulging himself by painting such an elaborate fringe. Notice how it is chaotically ornamental while the "fringe" of the horse''s mane and tale are in perfect synchronization with the overall action. You have captured here what rodeo (and civilization is all about) man trying to evoke the nature he feels separated from and then attempting to dominate it. I think this would be improved by cropping off some of the right, but even so I can''t in good conscience give this anything less than a 10.</td>', 'This is a great, great capture. It looks like a Picasso painting of a rodeo. Notice how the background is all texture. The horse looks like he''s praying. As he kneels into a prone position, the man is forced into a supine position, each being submissive in his own way. The fringe on the cowboy is excessive, but that becomes its own statement (perhaps on the feminine becoming masculine or the masculine becoming feminine or the sublime becoming ridiculous or the ridiculous becoming sublime... as we imagine the frilly cowboy when he is not in the middle of an intense act and mentally compare it to this one who is). I can imagine Picasso indulging himself by painting such an elaborate fringe. Notice how it is chaotically ornamental while the "fringe" of the horse''s mane and tale are in perfect synchronization with the overall action. You have captured here what rodeo (and civilization is all about) man trying to evoke the nature he feels separated from and then attempting to dominate it. I think this would be improved by cropping off some of the right, but even so I can''t in good conscience give this anything less than a 10.', '2007-04-07 15:06:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(3527787, 478477, 50695, '<td valign="top">very cool. 10. a simple, perfect composition. The diagonal of the shadow counters the diagonal of the sunlight, mirrored across a dark, thick dividing line. The divine S curve of the tracks is complemented by the curve of the person and the curve of the footsteps. Above the horizon we have a soft, subtle crosshatch. It is visually beautiful. Thematically, we ponder over how we approach darkness, how we face darkness, simply because we have to, simply because it is between us and home.</td>', 'very cool. 10. a simple, perfect composition. The diagonal of the shadow counters the diagonal of the sunlight, mirrored across a dark, thick dividing line. The divine S curve of the tracks is complemented by the curve of the person and the curve of the footsteps. Above the horizon we have a soft, subtle crosshatch. It is visually beautiful. Thematically, we ponder over how we approach darkness, how we face darkness, simply because we have to, simply because it is between us and home.', '2007-04-07 15:12:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(3527800, 483238, 50695, '<td valign="top">bizarre wonderful photo 10. That tree trunk is a great composition element emphasizing the "joke" and the fronds of the trees are visually delicious. The embrace, even though relegated to second string, is authentic and loving, so that we believe in the notion of "soulmates" this plays off of, and the title transcends punning to achieve metaphor (and I notice a visual similarity between the couple and the feet to match the verbal pun).</td>', 'bizarre wonderful photo 10. That tree trunk is a great composition element emphasizing the "joke" and the fronds of the trees are visually delicious. The embrace, even though relegated to second string, is authentic and loving, so that we believe in the notion of "soulmates" this plays off of, and the title transcends punning to achieve metaphor (and I notice a visual similarity between the couple and the feet to match the verbal pun).', '2007-04-07 15:16:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(3527801, 491117, 50695, '<td valign="top">wonderful textures. wow. I''ve never seen anything quite like this. 10</td>', 'wonderful textures. wow. I''ve never seen anything quite like this. 10', '2007-04-07 15:16:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(3527802, 488516, 50695, '<td valign="top">beautiful. stunning. 10</td>', 'beautiful. stunning. 10', '2007-04-07 15:16:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(3527810, 490206, 50695, '<td valign="top">This shows a bravery, an uncensored vision, that is missing from the kitschy ribbon winners of DPC that use similar lighting effects. You are not afraid of the dark. And you are not afraid of making us afraid of it. This is not a face I will soon forget. And unlike advertising and pornography (the two most imitated genres at DPC), she is looking at me more than I am looking at her. 10</td>', 'This shows a bravery, an uncensored vision, that is missing from the kitschy ribbon winners of DPC that use similar lighting effects. You are not afraid of the dark. And you are not afraid of making us afraid of it. This is not a face I will soon forget. And unlike advertising and pornography (the two most imitated genres at DPC), she is looking at me more than I am looking at her. 10', '2007-04-07 15:19:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(3527812, 480874, 50695, '<td valign="top">For the first two seconds I look at this picture, I think "so what." Then the cherry blossoms create an avalanche knocking me down into woman and dog. the tremendous step of the dog outside of the boundary of the walkway then sends me right out of the picture into a devastating mystery. This is what is meant by composition. This is what is meant by "the composition IS the subject." 10</td>', 'For the first two seconds I look at this picture, I think "so what." Then the cherry blossoms create an avalanche knocking me down into woman and dog. the tremendous step of the dog outside of the boundary of the walkway then sends me right out of the picture into a devastating mystery. This is what is meant by composition. This is what is meant by "the composition IS the subject." 10', '2007-04-07 15:22:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(3527813, 487101, 50695, '<td valign="top">be careful, that chaplin painting is so good it competes with your photograph. still, your composition and juxtaposition are just right, as are the b/w tones. you are clearly a master. 10</td>', 'be careful, that chaplin painting is so good it competes with your photograph. still, your composition and juxtaposition are just right, as are the b/w tones. you are clearly a master. 10', '2007-04-07 15:22:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(3527819, 487666, 50695, '<td valign="top">I cannot resist ghost trains. 10</td>', 'I cannot resist ghost trains. 10', '2007-04-07 15:26:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(3527824, 491069, 50695, '<td valign="top">this looks unreal, realer than real. 10</td>', 'this looks unreal, realer than real. 10', '2007-04-07 15:31:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(3527829, 488732, 50695, '<td valign="top">I hate pictures of cars. I hate negatives. So why do I love this? Because art is the combination of disparate elements into something completely new. 10</td>', 'I hate pictures of cars. I hate negatives. So why do I love this? Because art is the combination of disparate elements into something completely new. 10', '2007-04-07 15:33:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(3527831, 490433, 50695, '<td valign="top">they look like one winged creature! 10</td>', 'they look like one winged creature! 10', '2007-04-07 15:33:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(3527834, 490020, 50695, '<td valign="top">Yes, you really created something new from your environment. True photography, almost pure photography. 10</td>', 'Yes, you really created something new from your environment. True photography, almost pure photography. 10', '2007-04-07 15:34:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(3527840, 488414, 50695, '<td valign="top">almost too subtle even for me. but I love life on the edge. I think that this shot represents a globe with a satellite going around it... or a globe and an item in motion, since Galileo started the ball rolling on laws of motion. or a pendulum. this is truly camera obscura! 10</td>', 'almost too subtle even for me. but I love life on the edge. I think that this shot represents a globe with a satellite going around it... or a globe and an item in motion, since Galileo started the ball rolling on laws of motion. or a pendulum. this is truly camera obscura! 10', '2007-04-07 15:35:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(3527844, 484079, 50695, '<td valign="top">Thank you for allowing poor people to be happy. You truly have captured living spirit in a flat square. 10</td>', 'Thank you for allowing poor people to be happy. You truly have captured living spirit in a flat square. 10', '2007-04-07 15:36:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(3527848, 486598, 30850, '<td valign="top">The light in the lower right was distracting.  You might have cropped that out or edited it.</td>', 'The light in the lower right was distracting.  You might have cropped that out or edited it.', '2007-04-07 15:38:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(3527853, 490701, 50695, '<td valign="top">great title. is the light arriving or the darkness arriving? or is the man arriving. No, he''s departing. But departing into darkness or light? It is your offcenter composition with counteracting diagonals that creates all of this wonderful ambiguity. 10</td>', 'great title. is the light arriving or the darkness arriving? or is the man arriving. No, he''s departing. But departing into darkness or light? It is your offcenter composition with counteracting diagonals that creates all of this wonderful ambiguity. 10', '2007-04-07 15:39:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(3527854, 490928, 50695, '<td valign="top">It looks like he''s entering the photo, and in a sense he is. 10</td>', 'It looks like he''s entering the photo, and in a sense he is. 10', '2007-04-07 15:40:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(3527859, 487391, 50695, '<td valign="top">This is expert storytelling from another era, an American era somewhere around the 50s and 60s that never actually existed. 10</td>', 'This is expert storytelling from another era, an American era somewhere around the 50s and 60s that never actually existed. 10', '2007-04-07 15:44:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(3527861, 490908, 50695, '<td valign="top">I like how this somehow reminds me of an old-fashioned portrait. yet your title coyly implies that this is a candid, plus she is in very casual attire upon closer inspection. I like that tension between what''s there and what I think I''m seeing. 9</td>', 'I like how this somehow reminds me of an old-fashioned portrait. yet your title coyly implies that this is a candid, plus she is in very casual attire upon closer inspection. I like that tension between what''s there and what I think I''m seeing. 9', '2007-04-07 15:44:50.000000', NULL, 1),
