(3532498, 489867, 65319, '<td valign="top">I love the detail in this photo of your handsome son.  I often take photos of my kids with the flash on (even at the beach!) to get the "catch lights" in their eyes.</td>', 'I love the detail in this photo of your handsome son.  I often take photos of my kids with the flash on (even at the beach!) to get the "catch lights" in their eyes.', '2007-04-09 12:06:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(3532592, 489721, 70375, '<td valign="top">Okay, one thing that catches me right off is the tight crop and the busyness of the photograph. There is simply too much going on and one doesn''t know where to look first. Your colours are stunning though. Settings look good for the shot. Keep in mind that the natural inclination of the viewer is to look top right first and go clockwise from there. That may help. I hope so :)</td>', 'Okay, one thing that catches me right off is the tight crop and the busyness of the photograph. There is simply too much going on and one doesn''t know where to look first. Your colours are stunning though. Settings look good for the shot. Keep in mind that the natural inclination of the viewer is to look top right first and go clockwise from there. That may help. I hope so :)', '2007-04-09 12:47:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(3532603, 489571, 18780, '<td valign="top">Maybe, not enough contrast between the riders??</td>', 'Maybe, not enough contrast between the riders??', '2007-04-09 12:49:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(3532610, 490659, 68947, '<td valign="top">I thought this photo should have scored higher.  The traditional flower shots and lovely scenery shots are really nice, but there are not a lot of "deep" meanings to a lot of challenges and that seems to lend itself to a lot of boredom.  I LOVE the idea that you''ve done something different, other than a "technically perfect" shot or one of the traditional compositions.  We need more depth and artsy styles and particularily shots that have meaning, even if they are not "technically perfect" shots!</td>', 'I thought this photo should have scored higher.  The traditional flower shots and lovely scenery shots are really nice, but there are not a lot of "deep" meanings to a lot of challenges and that seems to lend itself to a lot of boredom.  I LOVE the idea that you''ve done something different, other than a "technically perfect" shot or one of the traditional compositions.  We need more depth and artsy styles and particularily shots that have meaning, even if they are not "technically perfect" shots!', '2007-04-09 12:51:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(3532616, 481971, 74979, '<td valign="top">Judy~ I also agree with SandyP; I think this shot was underrated.  this is (another) Lovely shot!  you have a gift of making flowers look more beautiful then they intrinsically are!  Strong work!</td>', 'Judy~ I also agree with SandyP; I think this shot was underrated.  this is (another) Lovely shot!  you have a gift of making flowers look more beautiful then they intrinsically are!  Strong work!', '2007-04-09 12:53:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(3532640, 480099, 42100, '<td valign="top">Wonderful light and composition.  I really like how each dog is its own photo and story, and yet they all work together for the photo as a whole(hope that makes sense).  Perfect DOF for this as well.  Excellent photo Linda!</td>', 'Wonderful light and composition.  I really like how each dog is its own photo and story, and yet they all work together for the photo as a whole(hope that makes sense).  Perfect DOF for this as well.  Excellent photo Linda!', '2007-04-09 13:01:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(3532667, 484800, 63269, '<td valign="top">Here''s my two cents. :)<br/> <br/>I like the color tones, and the atmosphere is really cool. Maybe the problem was a lack of composition... there isn''t a good emphasis on the subject. Something that would probably really help out is if you cropped out the distracing building thingy (whatever it is) on the right. Also, the focus should probably be on the horse, not the ground. <br/> <br/>Other than that, this photo looks like it has good potential... I kind of like it! :)</td>', 'Here''s my two cents. :) I like the color tones, and the atmosphere is really cool. Maybe the problem was a lack of composition... there isn''t a good emphasis on the subject. Something that would probably really help out is if you cropped out the distracing building thingy (whatever it is) on the right. Also, the focus should probably be on the horse, not the ground.  Other than that, this photo looks like it has good potential... I kind of like it! :)', '2007-04-09 13:09:22.000000', NULL, 0),
