(3534056, 490576, 27482, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by LanndonKane:</b></div><hr/><i> Just curious... How tall are those mountains?<br/>The image is so surreal I can''t really tell the true perspective. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Oh not tall at all, would rather classify them as hills rather than mountains, I don´t really have a good feel for height of landscape so take this with a grain of salt but probably only 50-100 meters higher than the ground below.</td>', 'Originally posted by LanndonKane: Just curious... How tall are those mountains?The image is so surreal I can''t really tell the true perspective.   Oh not tall at all, would rather classify them as hills rather than mountains, I don´t really have a good feel for height of landscape so take this with a grain of salt but probably only 50-100 meters higher than the ground below.', '2007-04-09 21:15:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(3534061, 487101, 50695, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Melethia:</b></div><hr/><i> I like the wide angle aspect of it - works quite well with the distortion, if you ask me. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>what she said. without the distortion there would have been even more "anxiety of influence" from the original painting.</td>', 'Originally posted by Melethia: I like the wide angle aspect of it - works quite well with the distortion, if you ask me.   what she said. without the distortion there would have been even more "anxiety of influence" from the original painting.', '2007-04-09 21:16:04.000000', NULL, 0),
