(3534852, 491093, 53814, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by TJinGuy:</b></div><hr/><i> I would be curious to know how you made the grass look like this. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Foreground (grass) blue channel was blended in "difference" mode with original RGB layer. Curves applied to lighten, then used the green channel from that for the final b/w. The background was selective gaussian blur on the original and then converted to b/w via channel mixer.<br/></td>', 'Originally posted by TJinGuy: I would be curious to know how you made the grass look like this.   Foreground (grass) blue channel was blended in "difference" mode with original RGB layer. Curves applied to lighten, then used the green channel from that for the final b/w. The background was selective gaussian blur on the original and then converted to b/w via channel mixer.', '2007-04-10 02:48:11.000000', NULL, 0),
