(3546866, 488755, 24454, '<td valign="top">OMG, this melted my heart immediately on impact!   What a great photo.  I bet his parents would love a print of this.  I sure would if that was my kid!  <br/> <br/>And I LOVE your framing.  I''m a border freak too and I always love the way you frame your photos.  I wish DPC wasn''t so psycho about that!!<br/> <br/>This is the kind of photo that will stay with me.  I''ll remember it even when I''m doing other things :)<br/></td>', 'OMG, this melted my heart immediately on impact!   What a great photo.  I bet his parents would love a print of this.  I sure would if that was my kid!   And I LOVE your framing.  I''m a border freak too and I always love the way you frame your photos.  I wish DPC wasn''t so psycho about that!! This is the kind of photo that will stay with me.  I''ll remember it even when I''m doing other things :)', '2007-04-14 02:24:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(3547013, 482979, 47541, '<td valign="top">Hi from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>Composition: The first thing that strikes me here is that you have broken one of the rules about composition and you have put your subject in the middle of the frame.  I guess you did this so that it is "framed" by the two industrial buildings?  I don''t think that was needed.  What would be better is to have the car to the left so it looks like it was driving through the shot.<br/> <br/>Technical:  The illusion of the car on the pipe is cool.  For DPC it isn''t so obvious without reading the notes.  I suggest you imply this in your title for the voters eg: "You take the road, I''ll take the pipe!"...or something like that.  The lighting feels a bit flat, some added contrast may help the shot.  If you have photoshop try playing with the Levels and Contrast adjustments on each image and see if it makes an improvement.  Other editing packages will have equivalents.<br/> <br/>Feel:  The idea of the car on the pipe is cool but the overall feel of the shot is a bit flat.  <br/> <br/>PM me if you have any questions</td>', 'Hi from the Critique Club! Composition: The first thing that strikes me here is that you have broken one of the rules about composition and you have put your subject in the middle of the frame.  I guess you did this so that it is "framed" by the two industrial buildings?  I don''t think that was needed.  What would be better is to have the car to the left so it looks like it was driving through the shot. Technical:  The illusion of the car on the pipe is cool.  For DPC it isn''t so obvious without reading the notes.  I suggest you imply this in your title for the voters eg: "You take the road, I''ll take the pipe!"...or something like that.  The lighting feels a bit flat, some added contrast may help the shot.  If you have photoshop try playing with the Levels and Contrast adjustments on each image and see if it makes an improvement.  Other editing packages will have equivalents. Feel:  The idea of the car on the pipe is cool but the overall feel of the shot is a bit flat.   PM me if you have any questions', '2007-04-14 06:07:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(3547018, 483689, 47541, '<td valign="top">Hi from the Critique Club.<br/> <br/>Composition: I love the composition in this.The teddy at the left with the baby forming a nice diagonal in the frame.  Great.<br/> <br/>Technical: The DOF seems to be nicely on the eyes but given you editing steps that may be an illusion.  In any case, the eyes are nicely done and the background is very nicely OOF.  There is a slight grain to the image which I''m unsure if I like or not.  The border is a bit think for my liking but thats just personal preference.<br/> <br/>Feel: I really like this shot, other than the border.  I can see why it scored as it did as DPC is not very baby photo friendly.  This is one that would look nice hanging on a wall.  Great work, like the rest of the portraits in your profile.<br/> <br/>PM if you have any queries</td>', 'Hi from the Critique Club. Composition: I love the composition in this.The teddy at the left with the baby forming a nice diagonal in the frame.  Great. Technical: The DOF seems to be nicely on the eyes but given you editing steps that may be an illusion.  In any case, the eyes are nicely done and the background is very nicely OOF.  There is a slight grain to the image which I''m unsure if I like or not.  The border is a bit think for my liking but thats just personal preference. Feel: I really like this shot, other than the border.  I can see why it scored as it did as DPC is not very baby photo friendly.  This is one that would look nice hanging on a wall.  Great work, like the rest of the portraits in your profile. PM if you have any queries', '2007-04-14 06:14:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(3547022, 489787, 47541, '<td valign="top">Hi from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>Composition: The composition is nice but something feels wrong.  It''s hard to put my finger on it but it could be that while the line between the pink and blue is level, where the wall meets the ground is not, or the balanced feel the pillar and bin gives the image.  In any case its not a major but a feeling.  I do like the shadow of the tree leading us to the seat and the nicely deliniated colours.<br/> <br/>Technical: Not much to say here as the image is mostly nice, simple, and clean.  Maybe a bit of cloning out of things such as the "lines" on the pillar near the top or some "things" on the ground.<br/> <br/>Feel:  I like the image but the score reflects that it doesn''t have a "wow" to it.  In a challenge with a topic that suited it better I am sure it would score closer to or over 6.<br/> <br/>Keep up the good work, this is a great effort for your first entry!  PM me if you have any queries.<br/></td>', 'Hi from the Critique Club! Composition: The composition is nice but something feels wrong.  It''s hard to put my finger on it but it could be that while the line between the pink and blue is level, where the wall meets the ground is not, or the balanced feel the pillar and bin gives the image.  In any case its not a major but a feeling.  I do like the shadow of the tree leading us to the seat and the nicely deliniated colours. Technical: Not much to say here as the image is mostly nice, simple, and clean.  Maybe a bit of cloning out of things such as the "lines" on the pillar near the top or some "things" on the ground. Feel:  I like the image but the score reflects that it doesn''t have a "wow" to it.  In a challenge with a topic that suited it better I am sure it would score closer to or over 6. Keep up the good work, this is a great effort for your first entry!  PM me if you have any queries.', '2007-04-14 06:22:13.000000', NULL, 0),
